<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="022" project="spaarke-daily-update-service-r5">
  <metadata>
    <title>Operator harness sign-off — approve one Daily Briefing variant (GATE G-R5-D, FR-D3)</title>
    <phase>D: Visual redesign</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>1</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>021</dependencies>
    <blocks>023</blocks>
    <tags>design, gate</tags>
    <rigor-hint>MINIMAL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Operator sign-off gate — no code implementation; records an approval decision and archives screenshots/spec.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical: present variants, record the operator's decision, archive artifacts. No design judgment by the agent (the operator judges).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Gate task — must run after 021 and before 023; blocks the port.</parallel-reason>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Present the task-021 Daily Briefing design variants to the operator and record which single variant is approved
    (GATE G-R5-D). Archive the approved screenshots and capture the approved design's concrete token/spacing/layout
    spec so task 023 can port it faithfully. This is an operator sign-off gate — do NOT self-approve.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE project facilitator. Presents the harness variants and their trade-offs to the operator, then records the
    operator's decision precisely. Does not substitute its own aesthetic judgment for the operator's.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Exactly one task-021 variant is operator-approved and recorded in
    projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/APPROVED.md, with the approved light+dark screenshots
    archived and the approved design's concrete token/spacing/layout spec captured for the task-023 port.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Per spec NFR-07, G-R5-D is satisfied by OPERATOR HARNESS SIGN-OFF (screenshots archived) — not by tests, curl,
      or logs. FR-D3 requires the redesign to be operator-approved IN THE HARNESS before any production change. This
      gate selects the single variant task 023 will port. Because the port must reproduce the approved look exactly,
      this task also captures the approved design's concrete spec (tokens, spacing scale, layout structure) rather
      than just "variant B".
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/variants-brief.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/ (per-variant light + dark screenshots)</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/APPROVED.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">This is an operator sign-off GATE. The agent MUST NOT self-approve, infer approval, or pick the variant on the operator's behalf. Approval is the operator's explicit decision recorded verbatim.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">If the operator is unavailable or does not respond, set this task's status to blocked (do NOT proceed to task 023). Record the blocked state and reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Exactly ONE variant is approved. If the operator asks for a blend or a revision instead of approving one as-is, record that as "revision requested", set status blocked, and route back to task 021 — do NOT record an approval.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The captured approved-design spec MUST be concrete enough to port: named Fluent v9 tokens, the spacing scale, the layout structure (regions/order), and where TL;DR + "Critical Today" sit. "Approved variant B" alone is insufficient.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">This task modifies ONLY files under projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/ (and TASK-INDEX.md). No source code.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/variants-brief.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="1">Compile a concise presentation for the operator: each task-021 variant with its light+dark screenshots and its parameter-by-parameter summary from variants-brief.md.</step>
    <step order="2">Present the variants to the operator and explicitly request selection of exactly one, using the format 🔔 Human Input Required (situation, options = the 2-3 variants, recommendation optional).</step>
    <step order="3">If the operator is unavailable OR requests a revision/blend rather than approving one variant: set this task's status to blocked, record the reason in notes/design/APPROVED.md, and STOP (do not proceed to task 023; route revision requests back to task 021).</step>
    <step order="4">On explicit approval of exactly one variant: write projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/APPROVED.md recording the approved variant id, the operator identity/date, and a link to the approved screenshots.</step>
    <step order="5">In APPROVED.md, capture the approved design's concrete port spec: named Fluent v9 tokens used, the spacing scale, the layout region structure and order, and the placement/prominence treatment of TL;DR and "Critical Today".</step>
    <step order="6">Copy the approved variant's light+dark screenshots into projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/approved/.</step>
    <step order="7">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status to completed (only if an approval was recorded).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>This entire task is a gate. If the operator does not explicitly approve exactly one variant, do NOT complete it — set status blocked and stop per root CLAUDE.md §6. Self-approval is forbidden.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands / copy screenshot files</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/APPROVED.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-daily-update-service-r5/notes/design/approved/ (approved light + dark screenshots)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The operator has explicitly approved exactly one variant (recorded verbatim; the agent did not self-approve).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/design/APPROVED.md records the approved variant id, the approving operator, the date, and links to the approved screenshots.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The approved light + dark screenshots are archived under notes/design/approved/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">APPROVED.md captures the approved design's concrete port spec — named Fluent v9 tokens, spacing scale, layout region structure/order, and TL;DR + "Critical Today" placement/prominence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If no approval was obtained (operator unavailable or revision requested), the task status is blocked and task 023 has not started.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No source code file is modified by this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    G-R5-D is an operator gate (spec NFR-07): screenshots + explicit approval, never tests/curl/logs. The concrete
    port spec in APPROVED.md is what makes the task-023 port faithful — without named tokens and layout structure the
    port will drift. Route revision/blend requests back to task 021 rather than recording a partial approval.
  </notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>
      Before starting this task, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;.
      Follow the task-execute skill for the mandatory pre-execution checklist.
    </protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
